      <revisionDesc>
          <change when="2024-02-26T11:07:58-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Finalized - Ready.</change>
          <change when="2023-12-20T06:51:31-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/simoeis">Vote - Accept-Straight-to-Finalization - Line 6: this is a good reading. Cf. the split tau in Sebastou, l. 15.  Verso l. 2: εἰς also looks good. Line 9: I see no reason for the regularization and would keep as is.  See Gonis's remark about the wrong page reference to Olsson.</change>
          <change when="2023-12-16T14:52:33-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Vote - DEFER - lin6 It could be κερμάτια, but dot tau. || v2 I cannot verify εἰς on the image. ἐπ’ οἴκο̣υ̣ B. Olsson, Papyrusbriefe p. 88 ('Papyrusbriefe 29' in a/c to r.5 refers to the number of the letter in this book; the page is still 88) </change>
          <change when="2023-12-15T05:14:45-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - Integration of BL corrections, additional corrections.</change>
          <change when="2023-12-15T05:10:41-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - I've integrated BL corrections and suggestions, and have added two more. In line 6 the tau of κερμάτια due to the lack of space at the end of the line was written as a fast ligature similar to the one in Σεβαστοῦ in line 15. On the verso, the expression is εἰς οἶκο(ν).</change>
